Cursor Rules — Faena AI Factory

Single source of truth: PROTOCOL.md at the repository root. Read it fully before acting; it holds the workspace invariants, the 5-step flow and the complete command surface.

Do not restate rules in this file. If the flow changes, edit PROTOCOL.md. scripts/validate-faena.ps1 fails if this file stops referencing it.

Host notes:
- Cursor loads .cursorrules on every request, so it stays deliberately small.
- For real Cursor project rules with globs, add thin shims in .cursor/rules/*.mdc that point at rules/*.md — never copies of the content.
- Users drag commands into chat as @commands/... or @tasks/task-.../...

Quick map: PROTOCOL.md (flow + invariants) | rules/process-task-list.md (TDD) | rules/skills-routing.md + skills/README.md (skills) | rules/project/ (company standards).
